# HTTP request templates, not terminal commands or previously executed requests.
# {{...}} marks placeholders; variable substitution syntax depends on the HTTP tool.
# Bind credentials only in the host's secure configuration. Never put a real key here.
# Fixed production API; no base URL variable or environment selection is required.

# Default read-only entry: this file contains only GET requests; offline checks do not execute them.
# Later network access requires separate authorization. Select only the needed request and never guess IDs.

### 1. Read-only authentication check without dialing
GET https://api.heycall-e.com/v1/goals?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{CALLE_API_KEY}}
Accept: application/json

### 2. List visible Goals; use next_cursor as after for pagination
GET https://api.heycall-e.com/v1/goals?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{CALLE_API_KEY}}
Accept: application/json

### 3. Read a known Goal without creating a Run
GET https://api.heycall-e.com/v1/goals/{{GOAL_ID}}
Authorization: Bearer {{CALLE_API_KEY}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Read a resource; CALL_RESOURCE_ID is the creation response's id, not the billing call_id
GET https://api.heycall-e.com/v2/calls/{{CALL_RESOURCE_ID}}
Authorization: Bearer {{CALLE_API_KEY}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Read events; use the corresponding cursor for the next page
GET https://api.heycall-e.com/v2/calls/{{CALL_RESOURCE_ID}}/events?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{CALLE_API_KEY}}
Accept: application/json

